## Set up a sine ratio
Let $h$ be the distance A swims. It is the hypotenuse; the lake width $100$ m is opposite the $55^\circ$ angle.
\sin 55^\circ &= \frac{100}{h}
## Solve for h
h &= \frac{100}{\sin 55^\circ}
h &= 122.077
h &= 122
ANSWER: 122 \text{ m}

## Write the sine rule for triangle ABC
Side $y$ is opposite the $30^\circ$ angle and the side $|AB| = 100$ is opposite the $105^\circ$ angle.
\frac{y}{\sin 30^\circ} &= \frac{100}{\sin 105^\circ}
## Solve for y
y &= \frac{100 \sin 30^\circ}{\sin 105^\circ}
y &\approx 51.7638
y &\approx 51.8
ANSWER: y = 51.8 \text{ m}

## Find h using triangle BCD
Triangle $BCD$ has a right angle at $D$. $h$ is opposite the $45^\circ$ angle and $y = 51.8$ is the hypotenuse.
\sin 45^\circ &= \frac{h}{51.8}
h &= 51.8 \sin 45^\circ
h &\approx 36.628
h &\approx 36.6
## Find x using triangle ACD
$h$ is opposite the $30^\circ$ angle and $x$ is the hypotenuse.
\sin 30^\circ &= \frac{36.6}{x}
x &= \frac{36.6}{\sin 30^\circ}
x &= 73.2
ANSWER: h = 36.6 \text{ m}, \quad x = 73.2 \text{ m}

## Add the seven yearly totals and divide by 7
m &= \frac{2779 + 3100 + 3175 + 3104 + 2825 + 2580 + 2547}{7}
m &= \frac{20110}{7}
m &\approx 2872.857
m &\approx 2872.9
