## Find a country with 0% in the gas column
Cyprus and Malta both show 0 for gas, so either is correct.
ANSWER: \text{Cyprus (or Malta)}

## Equate the rise in water to the volume of the ice
The volume of water that rises is a cylinder of radius 3.5 and height $h$. It equals the volume of 3 ice cubes.
\pi (3.5)^2 h &= 3\left(\frac{9\pi}{2}\right)
\pi (3.5)^2 h &= \frac{27\pi}{2}
## Divide both sides by pi
(3.5)^2 h &= \frac{27}{2}
## Solve for h
h &= \frac{27}{2(3.5)^2}
h &= \frac{27}{24.5}
h &\approx 1.102
h &\approx 1.1
ANSWER: h = 1.1 \text{ cm}

## Write the three face areas as equations
Each face area is the product of two of the dimensions.
xz &= 2\sqrt{2}
yz &= 8\sqrt{6}
xy &= 4\sqrt{3}
## Multiply the three equations
The volume is $xyz$, and the product of the three areas is $(xyz)^2$.
(xz)(yz)(xy) &= (2\sqrt{2})(8\sqrt{6})(4\sqrt{3})
x^2y^2z^2 &= 2 \times 8 \times 4 \times \sqrt{2 \times 6 \times 3}
&= 64\sqrt{36}
&= 64 \times 6
&= 384
## Take the square root to get the volume
xyz &= \sqrt{384}
&= \sqrt{64 \times 6}
&= 8\sqrt{6}
ANSWER: V = 8\sqrt{6}\ \text{cm}^3
